{
 "schema": "gpuwm-cm1.hurricane-runs/v1",
 "what": "What GM1's and CM1's runs of the hurricane presets did (CM1 r21.1's hurricane_3d_cpm case with the settings each preset's preset.json lists). The series are 3-hourly: the lowest pressure and the fastest ground-relative wind at the lowest model level (25 m), the radius of maximum wind (of the azimuthal-mean swirling wind at that level, about the pressure minimum), and the warm core (the azimuthal-mean potential temperature within 40 km of the centre minus the 300 to 450 km ring, at the height where that is largest) with that height, which moves from the middle of the column to near its top late in a run, so the warm-core numbers are two layers and not one curve. One script read every run's CM1-format frames.",
 "compared": {
  "gm1": "GM1 with a fixed 7.5 s time step (adapt_dt = 0, dtl = 7.5)",
  "cm1": "CM1 r21.1 run with the same changed settings but its own adaptive time step (from 10 s, as CM1's file has it)",
  "cm1_words": "adapt_dt = 1, dtl = 10",
  "note": "The time step is the one setting that differs between the two 8 km runs compared."
 },
