 "words": {
  "what_was_compared": "CM1 r21.1 run with the same changed settings but its own adaptive time step (from 10 s, as CM1's file has it); GM1 with a fixed 7.5 s time step",
  "known_issue_adaptive_step": "With CM1's own adaptive setting GM1's hurricane stops early or makes a much weaker storm, a known issue: 8 km runs on it stopped at hour 20.8 and at hour 29.1, and the one that ran to the end reached 995 hPa and 35 m/s ground-relative where CM1 reaches 955 hPa and 62 m/s ground-relative (measured with ArWen 2.8.0 (gpuwm 2.8.0)).",
  "card_8km_measured": "GM1's run of this preset on an RTX 4090 with ArWen 2.8.9 (gpuwm 2.8.9), on a fixed 7.5 s time step, is compared with a CM1 r21.1 run with the same changed settings but its own adaptive time step (from 10 s, as CM1's file has it). Through hour 54 the two stay within about 6 hPa and 7 m/s ground-relative at the lowest level. GM1 reaches 951.2 hPa at hour 90, with its fastest wind, 62.9 m/s ground-relative, at hour 93; CM1 reaches 954.9 hPa and 62.0 m/s ground-relative at hour 81. GM1's storm holds near its peak after it: 954.0 hPa and 58.8 m/s ground-relative at hour 96; CM1's storm weakens after it: 971.7 hPa and 50.7 m/s ground-relative at hour 96 (all measured).",
  "card_step": "The time step is a fixed 7.5 s where CM1's file has one that changes with the storm. With CM1's own adaptive setting GM1's hurricane stops early or makes a much weaker storm, a known issue: 8 km runs on it stopped at hour 20.8 and at hour 29.1, and the one that ran to the end reached 995 hPa and 35 m/s ground-relative where CM1 reaches 955 hPa and 62 m/s ground-relative (measured with ArWen 2.8.0 (gpuwm 2.8.0)).",
  "card_4km_measured": "GM1's run of this preset on an RTX 4090 with ArWen 2.8.9 (gpuwm 2.8.9) ran its whole 4 days: 989.6 hPa and 37.8 m/s ground-relative at the lowest level at hour 48, 965.6 hPa and 58.5 m/s ground-relative at hour 72, and 965.5 hPa and 52.4 m/s ground-relative at hour 96; it was strongest at hour 90, with 952.3 hPa and 69.9 m/s ground-relative (measured). The run with ArWen 2.8.0 (gpuwm 2.8.0) ended at 958.7 hPa and 61.8 m/s ground-relative. CM1 has not been run with these settings at 4 km, so this storm has nothing to be compared with.",
  "four_km_engine": "ArWen 2.8.9 (gpuwm 2.8.9)",
  "eye_basis_8km": "GM1's run of this preset on an RTX 4090 with ArWen 2.8.9 (gpuwm 2.8.9) has a clear eye and eyewall by hour 48, as a CM1 r21.1 run with the same changed settings but its own adaptive time step (from 10 s, as CM1's file has it) has (both measured)",
  "eye_basis_4km": "GM1's run of this preset on an RTX 4090 with ArWen 2.8.9 (gpuwm 2.8.9) has a clear eye by hour 48 (measured); CM1 has not been run with these settings at 4 km",
  "hours_81_to_96": "From hour 81 to hour 96 GM1's storm goes from 954.6 hPa and 61.4 m/s ground-relative to 954.0 hPa and 58.8 m/s ground-relative (in those hours its lowest pressure is 951.2 hPa, its fastest wind 62.9 m/s ground-relative, its radius of maximum wind 20 km throughout); CM1's goes from 954.9 hPa and 62.0 m/s ground-relative to 971.7 hPa and 50.7 m/s ground-relative (radius of maximum wind 20 to 28 km). So GM1's storm holds its strength through the last 15 hours while CM1's weakens (measured).",
  "tightening": "In both runs the radius of maximum wind is 20 km or less from hour 21: in GM1's run to the end (hour 96), in CM1's to hour 90, then 28 km (both measured, from the 3-hourly frames).",
  "time_8km": "On an RTX 4090 the 4 days took 24 minutes (46080 steps; other work shared the card for the first 12 minutes).",
  "warm_core": "Warm core: how much warmer the centre is than its surroundings, as potential temperature: the mean within 40 km of the centre (the mean of the averages around each ring one grid cell wide) minus the average of the 300 to 450 km ring, at the height where that difference is largest, and that height. The height is not the same all through a run: from hour 39 in GM1's run it is 7.8 to 8.8 km up through hour 78 and 13.3 to 15.3 km up from hour 81, and in CM1's run it is 8.2 to 9.2 km up through hour 72 and 11.8 to 15.8 km up from hour 75. A number from the middle of the storm and one from near its top are two different layers, so these numbers are not one curve: read a rise or a fall only between hours at about the same height."
 },
